From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:19:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/30] Split the replicated layer-input GEMVs across ranks
 behind G6_QA_SPLIT

G6_QA_SPLIT=1 runs each rank's 16-output tiles of q_a, kv_a, idx.wk and
idx.weights_proj (weights stay replicated; bind::narrow offsets the record
pointer and output columns) and all-gathers the columns per layer on a
fabric of its own (one collective per layer, port + 64) before the q_a
norm. G6_QA_SPLIT=2 splits q_a only and runs kv_a / idx in full while the
gather is on the wire. An output tile's arithmetic does not depend on which
tiles a launch covers, so the bits equal the replicated path. Default 0:
today's path unchanged.
